-- The example on explore.md: Alice and Bob each mean to buy dinner tonight,
-- and neither wants to buy it if the other already has. Alice checks whether
-- dinner is bought and, if her check found it unbought, buys. If Bob's
-- purchase is recorded between her check and her purchase, two dinners are
-- bought. That is a race condition, and this file is WRONG ON PURPOSE, so
-- that `l4 explore` has something to find. It models Alice's side only:
-- Bob's purchase is an act of the world, recorded by the dinner ledger.
--
-- Everything that can happen is one permission held by `World`, which
-- recurs on itself, and each act names its actor. Bob's purchase has to be
-- an act in the contract, or no exploration could vary when it lands: the
-- explorer tries only the acts that an obligation in force offers. Keep
-- the permission a MAY at every point. While a MUST or SHANT is pending in
-- it, the other actors' acts get no edge in that position, and nothing
-- says so (explore.md, "Loud and silent failures").

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    World      -- the one party that acts; each act names its actor
    Alice      -- whose own ledger holds what she believes

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`
    `Bob buys dinner`
    `Alice buys dinner`

DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    opened     -- nobody has bought dinner
    taken      -- Bob has

DECLARE Dinner IS ONE OF
    `dinner for two`

`closing` MEANS 100

§ `Reading the ledgers`

GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ledger is open` MEANS NOT (elem taken `dinner status record`)

GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A Status
`the ledger's status` MEANS
    IF elem taken `dinner status record` THEN taken ELSE opened

§ `The race`

GIVEN act IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dinner rules allow` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN (RECALL Alice's `belief`) EQUALS NOTHING
    WHEN `Bob buys dinner`                       THEN `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
    WHEN `Alice buys dinner`                     THEN (RECALL Alice's `belief`) EQUALS JUST opened
                                                      AND count (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinners bought`) EQUALS 0

-- The arrangement opens with dinner unbought: the ledger's first record.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the arrangement` MEANS
    COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
    HENCE `the evening`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the evening` MEANS
    PARTY World
    MAY   act PROVIDED `the dinner rules allow` act
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE CONSIDER act
          WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN
              RECORD Alice's `belief` IS `the ledger's status` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Bob buys dinner` THEN
              COMMIT `dinner status record` IS taken
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice buys dinner` THEN
              COMMIT `dinners bought` IS `dinner for two`
              HENCE COMMIT `open at acceptance` IS `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE `the evening`
    LEST  FULFILLED

§ `The property`

-- Safe means: a dinner is bought only if the ledger said unbought at the
-- instant the purchase took effect. `open at acceptance` holds one entry
-- per purchase, TRUE or FALSE. A property is an ordinary rule that gives a
-- BOOLEAN, and takes as inputs the ledger cells it reads, each named for
-- its cell.
GIVEN `open at acceptance` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every dinner was accepted while open` MEANS all (GIVEN ok YIELD ok) `open at acceptance`

-- Sequence A: Alice checks, Bob's purchase is recorded, Alice buys on what
-- her check told her. Two dinners.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 10
    PARTY World DOES `Bob buys dinner`                       AT 11
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                     AT 12
